<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia construction spending seen falling in '96.</title>
<headline>Malaysia construction spending seen falling in '96.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Capital expenditure in the construction sector is expected to decline by 50.9 percent in 1996, compared to a growth of 72.9 in 1995, the Ministry of Finance said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;This is in line with the expectation that, although construction activity will remain strong, new construction starts will not be as large as in 1995,&quot; the ministry said in its annual Economic Report.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom 603-201-4813</p>
</text>
